      "side": 1,
      "message": "The callers do not handle the new `FIB_PROTOCOL_MAX` result. For an oversized gateway on a paired interface, `lcp_router_route_path_parse()` passes it directly to `fib_proto_to_dpo()`, which hits `ASSERT(0)` in a debug build and returns zero (`DPO_PROTO_IP4`) in a release build. Since the address was reset, release builds then process a zero next hop instead of discarding the malformed path. The multicast prefix caller also passes an unchecked result to MFIB (or overwrites a failed group conversion with the source conversion). Could all callers propagate a conversion failure and reject the malformed route/path before invoking FIB/MFIB? Please add malformed gateway and multicast address regression coverage.",
      "tag": "prview:78efd46cc6d9bba6475d624c42e1b559:913307daedcc720fb0de901b8e73266598dbff3a",
      "revId": "913307daedcc720fb0de901b8e73266598dbff3a",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
