      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T10:55:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Setting `fp_len` to zero does not reject this route: `lcp_router_route_add()` and `lcp_router_route_del()` continue with the zeroed address and a valid IP protocol. An oversized destination therefore becomes `0.0.0.0/0` or `::/0`, so an add/replace can install or replace the default route, and a delete can remove an existing default route (IPv6 deletes the entire source entry). Libnl accepts oversized destination attributes, so this branch is reachable. Could this helper return an explicit failure and have both callers discard the message before any FIB/table changes? Please cover oversized IPv4/IPv6 destinations with regression tests that preserve an existing default route.",
      "tag": "prview:78efd46cc6d9bba6475d624c42e1b559:913307daedcc720fb0de901b8e73266598dbff3a",
